These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain lists. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

The two arXiv papers are The Promptware Kill Chain and Invitation Is All You Need. Lawfare covers the promptware kill chain, and the page's header also links Schneier on Security. SafeBreach's post covers the Gemini attack. Embrace The Red has two: the ZombAI post, and a later post on OpenAI's url_safe mitigations. Varonis's covers Reprompt. The last link is a Black Hat webinar.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org glossary and MITRE ATT&CK.

